  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wr100-900.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Wr 403.10 Earth Embankment Design Criteria",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wr 403.10 Earth Embankment Design Criteria. The department shall use one or more of the following texts in evaluating the competence of the submitted design:\n\n(a) USDA NRCS Earth Dams and Reservoirs Technical Release 210-60 (TR 210-60), 2019, available as noted in Appendix B;\n\n(b) Evaluation and Monitoring of Seepage and Internal Erosion” FEMA P-1032, May 2015, available as noted in Appendix B;\n\n(c) Filters for Embankment Dams – Best Practices for Design and Construction” FEMA,\n\n2011, available as noted in Appendix B;\n\n(d) “Technical Manual: Conduits through Embankment Dams” FEMA L-266, September 2005, available as noted in Appendix B;\n\n(e) “Technical Manual: Overtopping Protection for Dams” FEMA P-1015, 2014, available as noted in Appendix B;\n\n(f) “Technical Manual: Plastic Pipe Used in Embankment Dams” FEMA P-675, November 2007, available as noted in Appendix B; or\n\n(g) NRCS “National Engineering Handbook”, Part 628, Articulated Concrete Block Armored Spillways, March 2019, as noted in Appendix B.\n\nSource. #8414, eff 8-20-05; ss by #10510, eff 1-22-14; ss by #13980, eff 5-24-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wr100-900.html"
}
